5.161.m:
See whether somewhere, in some way, purification exists for him.
There is no sacred treatise that does not exist in this place;
no smṛti, no Purāṇa, or Vedānta, O best of the twice-born;
and there is no brahmin here who does not resemble an omniscient one.
Therefore, reflect quickly on that which will grant him purification,

5.167.m:
Subsisting on fruits and roots for the next three hundred years,
he stood contemplating the Supreme Brahman, O best of brāhmaṇas;
after that, he remained for an equal length of time subsisting on withered leaves.
